# SonarQube CLI Reference

> Full machine-readable docs: https://www.sonarsource.com/sonarqube/cli/llms.txt  
> Version: 1.3.0 | Source: https://github.com/SonarSource/sonarqube-cli

## Install

```bash
# macOS/Linux
curl -o- https://raw.githubusercontent.com/SonarSource/sonarqube-cli/refs/heads/master/user-scripts/install.sh | bash
```

## Authentication

```bash
sonar auth login                        # Browser-based login (must be run manually)
sonar auth login -s https://sonarcloud.io -o my-org   # SonarQube Cloud EU
sonar auth status                       # Verify active connection
sonar auth logout
```

## List Issues & Projects

```bash
sonar list projects                          # Discover available projects
sonar list projects -q my-project            # Filter by name/key
sonar list issues -p my-project              # All issues for a project
sonar list issues -p my-project --format toon  # LLM-optimized output (use this in agents)
sonar list issues -p my-project --statuses OPEN,CONFIRMED
sonar list issues -p my-project --severities HIGH,BLOCKER
```

## Analyze Code

```bash
# Secrets scanning
sonar analyze secrets src/config.ts
sonar analyze secrets src/file1.ts src/file2.ts
cat .env | sonar analyze secrets --stdin

# Dependency risks
sonar analyze dependency-risks -p my-project
sonar analyze dependency-risks -p my-project --statuses active --min-severity HIGH

# Agentic analysis (SonarQube Cloud only)
sonar analyze agentic                        # Changed files vs git diff
sonar analyze agentic --staged               # Staged files only
sonar analyze agentic --base main            # Files changed vs main branch
sonar analyze agentic --file src/foo.ts      # Specific file
sonar analyze agentic --depth DEEP           # Cross-file analysis (default for multi-file)
```

## Remediate Issues

```bash
sonar remediate -p my-project                # Interactive — pick issues to fix
sonar remediate -p my-project --issues AYx1z2,AYx1z3   # Non-interactive (max 20)
```

## Cursor Integration

```bash
sonar integrate cursor -p my-project         # Project-level: MCP + hooks + Vortex
sonar integrate cursor -g                    # Global: installs to ~/.cursor
sonar integrate git                          # Pre-commit secrets scan hook
sonar integrate git --hook pre-push --global
```

## Direct API Access

```bash
sonar api get "/api/rules/search?languages=ts"
sonar api post "/api/issues/do_transition" --data '{"issue":"AYx1z2","transition":"accept"}'
sonar api get "/api/system/status" --verbose
```

## System & Updates

```bash
sonar system status         # Show auth, installed binaries, integrations
sonar self-update           # Update CLI to latest version
sonar self-update --status  # Check for newer version without installing
sonar system reset          # Factory reset (removes tokens, binaries, cache)
```

## Tips for Agents

- Use `--format toon` with `sonar list issues` for LLM-friendly output.
- `sonar auth login` cannot be automated — it opens a browser. Use env vars for CI.
- Prefer `sonar analyze agentic --base main` to scope analysis to your branch's changes.
- `DEEP` depth analysis catches cross-file issues; use `STANDARD` for faster single-file checks.
